---
title: Homemade Pizza Pockets
source: direct-input
cook time: 7-10 minutes
---

Preheat your oven to 400°F (200°C). Lightly dust a clean, dry work surface with @flour{}.

Unroll the @Pillsbury pizza crust{1%can} onto the floured surface. The dough may be sticky, so you can dust your hands with flour as well. Gently stretch or roll the dough if needed. 

Use a knife or pizza cutter to slice the dough in half lengthwise. Then, cut each half crosswise into three even strips. You should end with 6 rectangular pieces of dough.

Take one piece of dough and gently stretch or press it slightly. Spoon @pizza sauce{1-2%tbsp} onto one half of the rectangle, leaving a clear border (about ½ inch) around the edges. Add a layer of @mozzarella cheese{1 ½-2%cups} and your chosen toppings, like @pepperoni{30-40%slices}. Don't overfill, or it will be hard to seal and may leak. 

Carefully fold the empty half of the dough over the filling to create a rectangle pocket. Press the edges down firmly with your fingers. To ensure a good seal, you can gently press or crimp the edges with a fork.

In a small bowl, whisk together @egg{1%large} and @water{1%tsp}. For extra flavor, mix in optional seasonings like @?Italian seasoning{} or @?garlic powder{} or @?oregano{}. Brush the top of each sealed pocket with the egg wash. This will give them a golden, shiny finish.

Place the pockets on a #baking sheet{}. Bake in the preheated oven for ~{7-10%minutes}, or until the pockets are puffed up and golden brown.

Let the hot pockets cool for a few minutes after removing them from the oven (the filling will be very hot!). Cut one open to check, then serve warm.
